&sect;5

And this is the aspect of Pesach, matzah, and maror. And this is the aspect of the mitzvah of telling the story of Yetzias Mitzrayim, which is the aspect of Pesach &mdash; peh sach [&ldquo;the mouth speaks&rdquo;]. For this is the essential thing: to speak of all His wonders and to tell at length about this, as it is written: &ldquo;And whoever tells at length about Yetzias Mitzrayim &mdash; behold, this is praiseworthy.&rdquo;

For the voice of the melody is very, very precious and has a great power to arouse a person &mdash; that is, to arouse the minds, in the aspect of: &ldquo;The voice arouses the kavanah&rdquo; (Berachos 24b). But the essential completeness of the voice is when one connects it to the dibbur [speech] with a firm and strong connection. For this is the essential aspect of the totality of all the yichudim [unifications] &mdash; to unify and connect the voice with the speech, as is understood from the holy Zohar and from the words of our master, our teacher, and our rabbi, of blessed memory, in the Torah teaching &ldquo;Sason v&rsquo;simchah yimatzai vah&rdquo; (siman 178).
